+> STOP. Captain's notes: non-binding. Captain writes, Captain trims. Anyone else: close this file now.
+
+# Captain Notes
+
+Binding behaviour lives in `.feature` specs and referenced `assets/**`. History lives in git. These notes carry only what the next cycle needs.
+
+## Current Voyage
+
+Greenfield TodoMVC build. Vanilla JavaScript. localStorage persistence. Routing via hash. Base markup from `assets/app-template.index.html`. Spec from `assets/app-spec.md`.
+
+## Stack
+
+Vanilla JavaScript (no preprocessors). Cucumber + happy-dom for verification. npm for packages.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- `index.html` goes to project root, not a subfolder.
+- `js/app.js` is a single file; no models/controllers split needed for vanilla JS.
+- CSS files served from `node_modules/todomvc-common/base.css` and `node_modules/todomvc-app-css/index.css` per the template markup; a local `css/app.css` for overrides.
+- localStorage key: `todos-vanillajs`.
+- Routing: hash-based (`#/`, `#/active`, `#/completed`). No routing library needed; vanilla `hashchange` listener suffices.
+- Tier: happy-dom (cheapest sufficient to observe DOM-level behaviour).
diff --git a/specs/todos-clearing.feature b/specs/todos-clearing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..688c138
--- /dev/null
+++ b/specs/todos-clearing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@
+Feature: Clear completed todos
+  As a user
+  I want to remove all completed todos at once
+  So that I can tidy up my list
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is open
+
+  Rule: Clear completed button visibility
+
+    Scenario: Clear completed button hidden when no completed todos
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the clear-completed button is hidden
+
+    Scenario: Clear completed button visible when completed todos exist
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the todo at position 1 is completed
+      Then the clear-completed button is visible
+
+    Scenario: Clear completed button hidden when all todos removed
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the todo at position 1 is completed
+      When the user destroys the todo at position 1
+      Then the clear-completed button is hidden
+
+  Rule: Clearing completed todos
+
+    Scenario: Clear completed removes only completed todos
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has added a todo "Walk dog"
+      And the user has added a todo "Read book"
+      And the todo at position 1 is completed
+      And the todo at position 3 is completed
+      When the user clicks clear-completed
+      Then the todo list contains 1 item
+      And the todo at position 1 has title "Walk dog"
+
+    Scenario: Clear completed resets toggle-all checkbox
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And all todos are completed
+      When the user clicks clear-completed
+      Then the todo list contains 0 items
+      And the toggle-all checkbox is not checked
+
+    Scenario: Clear completed hides footer when all todos removed
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the todo at position 1 is completed
+      When the user clicks clear-completed
+      Then the footer is hidden
diff --git a/specs/todos-counter.feature b/specs/todos-counter.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..94858a3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/specs/todos-counter.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+Feature: Active todo counter
+  As a user
+  I want to see how many active todos I have
+  So that I know how much work remains
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is open
+
+  Rule: Counter displays active count
+
+    Scenario: Counter shows zero items when no todos exist
+      Given there are no todos
+      Then the counter text is "0 items left"
+
+    Scenario: Counter shows singular for one active todo
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the counter text is "1 item left"
+
+    Scenario: Counter shows plural for multiple active todos
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has added a todo "Walk dog"
+      Then the counter text is "2 items left"
+
+    Scenario: Counter excludes completed todos
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has added a todo "Walk dog"
+      And the todo at position 1 is completed
+      Then the counter text is "1 item left"
+
+    Scenario: Counter shows zero when all todos are completed
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And all todos are completed
+      Then the counter text is "0 items left"
+
+  Rule: Counter updates on toggle
+
+    Scenario: Counter updates when a todo is completed
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has added a todo "Walk dog"
+      When the user toggles the todo at position 1
+      Then the counter text is "1 item left"
+
+    Scenario: Counter updates when a todo is unchecked
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the todo at position 1 is completed
+      When the user toggles the todo at position 1
+      Then the counter text is "1 item left"
diff --git a/specs/todos-editing.feature b/specs/todos-editing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4baf20d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/specs/todos-editing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@
+Feature: Edit a todo
+  As a user
+  I want to change the title of a todo
+  So that I can correct mistakes or update tasks
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is open
+
+  Rule: Activating edit mode
+
+    Scenario: Double-click enters editing mode
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      When the user double-clicks the todo at position 1
+      Then the todo at position 1 has class "editing"
+      And the edit input at position 1 has value "Buy milk"
+      And the edit input at position 1 is focused
+
+  Rule: Saving edits
+
+    Scenario: Pressing Enter saves the edit
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user is editing the todo at position 1
+      When the user clears the edit input and types "Buy oat milk"
+      And the user presses Enter to confirm
+      Then the todo at position 1 has title "Buy oat milk"
+      And the todo at position 1 does not have class "editing"
+
+    Scenario: Blurring saves the edit
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user is editing the todo at position 1
+      When the user clears the edit input and types "Buy oat milk"
+      And the user blurs the edit input
+      Then the todo at position 1 has title "Buy oat milk"
+      And the todo at position 1 does not have class "editing"
+
+    Scenario: Empty edit destroys the todo
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user is editing the todo at position 1
+      When the user clears the edit input
+      And the user presses Enter to confirm
+      Then the todo list contains 0 items
+
+    Scenario: Empty edit on blur destroys the todo
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user is editing the todo at position 1
+      When the user clears the edit input
+      And the user blurs the edit input
+      Then the todo list contains 0 items
+
+  Rule: Cancelling edits
+
+    Scenario: Escape discards changes
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user is editing the todo at position 1
+      When the user clears the edit input and types "Something else"
+      And the user presses Escape
+      Then the todo at position 1 has title "Buy milk"
+      And the todo at position 1 does not have class "editing"
diff --git a/specs/todos-lifecycle.feature b/specs/todos-lifecycle.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..128cfbd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/specs/todos-lifecycle.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@
+Feature: Todo lifecycle
+  As a user
+  I want to create, view, and remove todos
+  So that I can track tasks I need to accomplish
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is open
+
+  Rule: Empty state
+
+    Scenario: No todos hides main and footer
+      Given there are no todos
+      Then the main section is hidden
+      And the footer is hidden
+
+  Rule: Adding todos
+
+    Scenario: New todo appears on Enter
+      Given the todo input is focused
+      When the user types "Buy milk" and presses Enter
+      Then the todo list contains 1 item
+      And the todo at position 1 has title "Buy milk"
+      And the todo at position 1 is not completed
+      And the todo input is empty
+
+    Scenario: Empty input is discarded on Enter
+      Given the todo input is focused
+      When the user types "   " and presses Enter
+      Then the todo list contains 0 items
+
+    Scenario: Leading and trailing whitespace is trimmed
+      Given the todo input is focused
+      When the user types "  Buy milk  " and presses Enter
+      Then the todo at position 1 has title "Buy milk"
+
+    Scenario: New todo input is cleared after adding
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the todo input is empty
+
+    Scenario: Adding a todo reveals main and footer
+      Given there are no todos
+      When the user adds a todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the main section is visible
+      And the footer is visible
+
+  Rule: Removing todos
+
+    Scenario: Destroy button removes a todo
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has added a todo "Walk dog"
+      When the user destroys the todo at position 1
+      Then the todo list contains 1 item
+      And the todo at position 1 has title "Walk dog"
+
+    Scenario: Removing all todos restores empty state
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      When the user destroys the todo at position 1
+      Then the todo list contains 0 items
+      And the main section is hidden
+      And the footer is hidden
diff --git a/specs/todos-persistence.feature b/specs/todos-persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ebbbd54
--- /dev/null
+++ b/specs/todos-persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+Feature: Persist todos to localStorage
+  As a user
+  I want my todos to survive page reloads
+  So that I do not lose my task list
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is open
+
+  Rule: Storage on change
+
+    Scenario: Todos are saved to localStorage after adding
+      When the user adds a todo "Buy milk"
+      Then localStorage contains a key "todos-vanillajs"
+      And localStorage "todos-vanillajs" contains a todo with title "Buy milk" and completed false
+
+    Scenario: Toggle state is persisted
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      When the user toggles the todo at position 1
+      Then localStorage "todos-vanillajs" contains a todo with title "Buy milk" and completed true
+
+    Scenario: Removed todo is not in localStorage
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has added a todo "Walk dog"
+      When the user destroys the todo at position 1
+      Then localStorage "todos-vanillajs" does not contain a todo with title "Buy milk"
+      And localStorage "todos-vanillajs" contains a todo with title "Walk dog" and completed false
+
+  Rule: Restoration on load
+
+    Scenario: Todos are restored from localStorage on page load
+      Given localStorage "todos-vanillajs" contains a todo with title "Buy milk" and completed false
+      And localStorage "todos-vanillajs" contains a todo with title "Walk dog" and completed true
+      When the app reloads
+      Then the todo list contains 2 items
+      And the todo at position 1 has title "Buy milk"
+      And the todo at position 1 is not completed
+      And the todo at position 2 has title "Walk dog"
+      And the todo at position 2 is completed
+
+    Scenario: Editing mode is not persisted
+      Given localStorage "todos-vanillajs" contains a todo with title "Buy milk" and completed false
+      When the app reloads
+      Then the todo at position 1 does not have class "editing"
diff --git a/specs/todos-routing.feature b/specs/todos-routing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..307b4f2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/specs/todos-routing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@
+Feature: Filter todos by route
+  As a user
+  I want to filter my todo list by status
+  So that I can focus on active or completed items
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is open
+
+  Rule: Default route shows all
+
+    Scenario: All todos are visible on the default route
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has added a todo "Walk dog"
+      And the todo at position 1 is completed
+      When the user navigates to "#/"
+      Then the todo list shows 2 visible items
+
+  Rule: Active filter
+
+    Scenario: Active route shows only active todos
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has added a todo "Walk dog"
+      And the todo at position 1 is completed
+      When the user navigates to "#/active"
+      Then the todo list shows 1 visible item
+      And the visible todo at position 1 has title "Walk dog"
+
+    Scenario: Active filter link is selected
+      When the user navigates to "#/active"
+      Then the "Active" filter link has class "selected"
+
+  Rule: Completed filter
+
+    Scenario: Completed route shows only completed todos
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has added a todo "Walk dog"
+      And the todo at position 1 is completed
+      When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+      Then the todo list shows 1 visible item
+      And the visible todo at position 1 has title "Buy milk"
+
+    Scenario: Completed filter link is selected
+      When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+      Then the "Completed" filter link has class "selected"
+
+  Rule: All filter link
+
+    Scenario: All filter link is selected on default route
+      When the user navigates to "#/"
+      Then the "All" filter link has class "selected"
+
+  Rule: Dynamic filter updates
+
+    Scenario: Completing a todo hides it from active filter
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has added a todo "Walk dog"
+      When the user navigates to "#/active"
+      And the user toggles the todo at position 1
+      Then the todo list shows 1 visible item
+      And the visible todo at position 1 has title "Walk dog"
diff --git a/specs/todos-toggle.feature b/specs/todos-toggle.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6fc8379
--- /dev/null
+++ b/specs/todos-toggle.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@
+Feature: Toggle todo completion
+  As a user
+  I want to mark todos as complete or active
+  So that I can track my progress
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is open
+
+  Rule: Individual toggle
+
+    Scenario: Clicking checkbox marks a todo as completed
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      When the user toggles the todo at position 1
+      Then the todo at position 1 is completed
+
+    Scenario: Clicking checkbox again marks a todo as active
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the todo at position 1 is completed
+      When the user toggles the todo at position 1
+      Then the todo at position 1 is not completed
+
+    Scenario: Completed todo has the completed class
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      When the user toggles the todo at position 1
+      Then the todo at position 1 has class "completed"
+
+  Rule: Mark all as complete
+
+    Scenario: Toggle-all checks all todos
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has added a todo "Walk dog"
+      When the user toggles all todos on
+      Then the todo at position 1 is completed
+      And the todo at position 2 is completed
+      And the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+    Scenario: Toggle-all unchecks all todos
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has added a todo "Walk dog"
+      And all todos are completed
+      When the user toggles all todos off
+      Then the todo at position 1 is not completed
+      And the todo at position 2 is not completed
+      And the toggle-all checkbox is not checked
+
+    Scenario: Toggle-all reflects state when all items are checked
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has added a todo "Walk dog"
+      When the user toggles the todo at position 1
+      And the user toggles the todo at position 2
+      Then the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+    Scenario: Toggle-all unchecks when one item is unchecked
+      Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has added a todo "Walk dog"
+      And all todos are completed
+      When the user toggles the todo at position 1
+      Then the toggle-all checkbox is not checked
